  return bio11Svg('bio11-fig-2-7', '0 0 1110 300', 'Fig: 2.7 Formation of disaccharides from monosaccharides monomers', 'Glucose (C6H12O6, a six-membered ring) and fructose (C6H12O6, a five-membered ring) combine by synthesis to give sucrose (C12H22O11) plus water; hydrolysis is the reverse. In general, monosaccharide plus monosaccharide gives disaccharide plus water.', body, 'background:#fff');
